{
  "info": {
    "name": "L09ClientMCP - Branch 7: SSE Transport Integration",
    "description": "Branch 7: SSE Transport Integration for External MCP Servers\n\nThis collection demonstrates the evolution from mock in-process MCP server (Branch 6) to real external MCP server communication using SSE (Server-Sent Events) transport (Branch 7).\n\n## Key Learning Objectives\n- Real network-based MCP communication patterns\n- SSE transport layer implementation and testing\n- External server integration and health monitoring\n- Configuration-driven server connections\n- Production-ready error handling and retry logic\n\n## Architecture Evolution\n**Branch 6**: Spring AI Functions → Mock Echo Server (in-process)\n**Branch 7**: Spring AI Functions → SSE Client → External MCP Server (network)\n\n## Testing Scenarios\n1. **External Server Health**: Verify external MCP server is running and accessible\n2. **SSE Connection Status**: Check SSE transport layer connectivity\n3. **Tool Discovery**: Validate tool listing from external server\n4. **Function Integration**: Test Spring AI function calls using external tools\n5. **Network Error Handling**: Verify graceful degradation when server unavailable\n6. **Configuration Testing**: Validate SSE transport configuration\n\n## Prerequisites\n- External MCP server running on localhost:3000\n- Spring application configured with SSE transport\n- spring.ai.mcp.client.type=SYNC in application.yml\n\n## Educational Value\nThis collection teaches:\n- Real distributed system communication patterns\n- Network error handling and retry mechanisms\n- External service integration testing strategies\n- SSE protocol understanding and debugging\n- Production-ready MCP client implementation patterns",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health Checks",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Spring App Health Check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Branch 7: Validate Spring application health with SSE transport",
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Response contains health status\", function () {",
                  "    const responseText = pm.response.text();",
                  "    pm.expect(responseText).to.include(\"MCP\");",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Branch 7 Enhancement: Check for SSE transport indicators",
                  "pm.test(\"Health response indicates SSE transport (Branch 7)\", function () {",
                  "    const responseText = pm.response.text();",
                  "    // Should show SSE connection status",
                  "    console.log(\"📡 Spring Health Status:\", responseText);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "console.log(\"🔍 Branch 7: Spring application health validated\");",
                  "console.log(\"📊 Next: Check external MCP server connectivity\");"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/chat/health",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "chat", "health"]
            }
